{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "Read by src-tauri/src/audio/drum_map.rs and src/audio/drum-map.test.ts so the Rust and TypeScript drum map rules cannot drift. `validity` cases say whether a mix carrying that `drumMap` must be accepted; `resolution` cases give, for a map and whether the track is percussion, the key each [key, articulation id or null] hit plays (null: no sound). `presets` cases give an embedded presets file and the presets that survive it: a preset that is malformed anywhere (its id, `rows` or one row) is dropped as a whole and reported, and the others survive, on both sides. `nativeOnly` holds forms that the native loader refuses and TypeScript cannot tell apart after JSON.parse: a number written as a float (38.0, 1e2) is an integer to JSON.parse, so only the native loader (the loader of record) can refuse it; the persisted writer never writes one. TypeScript's test pins that it reads each as the integer, so the difference stays exactly this list.",
